WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.510 --> 00:00:03.310
At last, mom and dad are back together.

00:00:03.310 --> 00:00:07.270
That's right, Marvel friends and fiends: Sony
Pictures, Marvel Studios, and the Walt Disney

00:00:07.270 --> 00:00:11.800
Company have finally set aside their differences,
returned to the negotiation table, and agreed

00:00:11.800 --> 00:00:13.890
to make a third Spider-Man movie together.

00:00:13.890 --> 00:00:16.400
"Let's try that again."

00:00:16.400 --> 00:00:20.280
Sony and Marvel confirmed on Friday, September
27th that an agreement had been reached to

00:00:20.280 --> 00:00:24.880
allow Marvel Studios president Kevin Feige
to produce another Spidey flick to follow

00:00:24.880 --> 00:00:29.970
2017's Spider-Man: Homecoming and 2019's Spider-Man:
Far From Home.

00:00:29.970 --> 00:00:34.019
This means that the ever-charming Tom Holland,
the third actor to step into the Spider-Man

00:00:34.019 --> 00:00:38.590
suit and the man largely considered the best
Peter Parker yet, will indeed swing back into

00:00:38.590 --> 00:00:42.769
the Marvel Cinematic Universe and reprise
his role as the friendly neighborhood hero.

00:00:42.769 --> 00:00:47.690
"That's what it said on the news, and the
news never lies."

00:00:47.690 --> 00:00:51.979
The peace-restoring meeting happened just
recently, with Marvel, Sony, and Disney executives

00:00:51.979 --> 00:00:55.829
inking the new deal on the evening of Thursday,
September 26th.

00:00:55.829 --> 00:00:59.549
An important aspect of this agreement is,
of course, the money, which is something that

00:00:59.549 --> 00:01:02.379
contributed to Sony and Marvel splitting in
the first place.

00:01:02.379 --> 00:01:07.030
On August 20th, 2019, it was announced that
the two studios were unable to see eye-to-eye

00:01:07.030 --> 00:01:12.890
on how to rework their 2015 deal that gave
Feige producing power in the Spider-Man franchise,

00:01:12.890 --> 00:01:16.890
let Holland's Spider-Man appear in Marvel
movies, and granted Disney, which owns Marvel

00:01:16.890 --> 00:01:22.390
Studios, five percent of day-one box office
profits as well as all merchandising revenue.

00:01:22.390 --> 00:01:27.140
Disney reportedly requested a 50 percent co-financing
stake in the franchise, which Sony is said

00:01:27.140 --> 00:01:28.670
to have denied outright.

00:01:28.670 --> 00:01:32.310
Though subsequent reports claimed that the
House of Mouse actually asked for a 30 percent

00:01:32.310 --> 00:01:37.200
share, it was evident that money was making
both studios more than a little tense.

00:01:42.820 --> 00:01:44.400
"Now get outta here."

00:01:44.400 --> 00:01:48.690
Thankfully, Sony, Disney, and Marvel brass
have now agreed that the latter two companies

00:01:48.690 --> 00:01:53.270
will receive 25 percent of the profits on
the third Spider-Man movie, with Sony retaining

00:01:53.270 --> 00:01:54.440
75 percent.

00:01:54.440 --> 00:01:57.960
Additionally, Disney will continue earning
merchandising profits.

00:01:57.960 --> 00:02:01.760
This newly confirmed third Spider-Man movie
doesn't yet have a title, but it does have

00:02:01.760 --> 00:02:04.980
a release date: July 16, 2021.

00:02:04.980 --> 00:02:09.619
It also has Homecoming and Far From Home producer
Amy Pascal on board to continue her producing

00:02:09.619 --> 00:02:10.619
role.

00:02:10.619 --> 00:02:14.870
Feige expressed gratitude and excitement about
the new deal being struck, saying in a statement

00:02:14.870 --> 00:02:16.300
released alongside the news,

00:02:16.300 --> 00:02:20.880
"I am thrilled that Spidey's journey in the
MCU will continue, and I and all of us at

00:02:20.880 --> 00:02:24.239
Marvel Studios are very excited that we get
to keep working on it.

00:02:24.239 --> 00:02:29.040
Spider-Man is a powerful icon and hero whose
story crosses all ages and audiences around

00:02:29.040 --> 00:02:30.040
the globe."

00:02:30.040 --> 00:02:32.800
Unsurprisingly, Pascal felt the same way,
saying,

00:02:32.800 --> 00:02:34.099
"This is terrific.

00:02:34.099 --> 00:02:37.930
Peter Parker's story took a dramatic turn
in Far From Home and I could not be happier

00:02:37.930 --> 00:02:41.629
we will all be working together as we see
where his journey goes."

00:02:41.629 --> 00:02:45.340
Perhaps the best part of this news is that
the upcoming movie isn't the only project

00:02:45.340 --> 00:02:48.239
Holland is going to be a part of at the House
of Heroes.

00:02:48.239 --> 00:02:52.560
According to Variety, the new agreement between
Sony and Marvel details that Holland's Spider-Man

00:02:52.560 --> 00:02:55.900
will appear in at least one future Marvel
Studios film.

00:02:55.900 --> 00:02:56.900
"Oh.

00:02:56.900 --> 00:02:58.489
This is nice."

00:02:58.489 --> 00:03:00.909
Holland also has a bright future ahead at
Sony.

00:03:00.909 --> 00:03:05.370
When the Sony-Marvel divorce was first confirmed,
it was reported that Holland was contracted

00:03:05.370 --> 00:03:07.659
for two future films under Sony Pictures.

00:03:07.659 --> 00:03:12.109
Now, it stands to reason that one of those
projects is the third Spider-Man movie everyone's

00:03:12.109 --> 00:03:15.040
freaking out about right now, but what about
the other one?

00:03:15.040 --> 00:03:19.069
It doesn't seem as though it's the forthcoming
Marvel movie Holland's now slated for, since

00:03:19.069 --> 00:03:21.950
that project is housed at a completely different
studio.

00:03:21.950 --> 00:03:23.379
So, what could that be?

00:03:23.379 --> 00:03:27.900
Thanks to a tease from Feige himself, it's
likely that yet another movie Holland's Spider-Man

00:03:27.900 --> 00:03:32.579
will be in is one under the umbrella of Sony's
Spider-Verse, which includes Spider-Man: Into

00:03:32.579 --> 00:03:37.879
the Spider-Verse, Venom, and the impending
films Venom 2, Morbius, and Kraven the Hunter.

00:03:37.879 --> 00:03:38.939
As Feige dished,

00:03:38.939 --> 00:03:42.959
"[Spider-Man] also happens to be the only
hero with the superpower to cross cinematic

00:03:42.959 --> 00:03:47.310
universes, so as Sony continues to develop
their own Spidey-verse you never know what

00:03:47.310 --> 00:03:49.299
surprises the future might hold."

00:03:49.299 --> 00:03:54.359
All in all, September 27th, 2019 will go down
in history as a victorious day for the folks

00:03:54.359 --> 00:03:59.489
at Sony, Disney, and Marvel, as well as for
fans of Spider-Man, the MCU, and Tom Holland

00:03:59.489 --> 00:04:00.540
himself.

00:04:00.540 --> 00:04:04.810
Now that the web-slinger has officially returned
to the MCU, the only thing left to do is figure

00:04:04.810 --> 00:04:07.080
out a name for the new Spider-Man movie.

00:04:07.080 --> 00:04:09.389
How about "Spider-Man: Home Sweet Home"?

00:04:09.389 --> 00:04:13.870
"That is literally the coolest sentence anyone
has ever said."

